help.start() instead of via the (by R automatically) generated PDFs.
That way you can more easily follow links between functions and across
packages.  So, in your case you'll get to there by:

help("CbsModel")

> I see that it has inherited a method called
> extractRawCopyNumbers() from ChromosomalModel. So I go to the documentation
> about ChromosomalModel,

I think you meant CopyNumberChromosomalModel, which you can click to
from the CbsModel help page.

> find that it has the method extractRawCopyNumbers()

which help page you can click to from the latter page.

> but I cannot find what arguments you need to use for this method, which
> values these arguments might have, what the return type of this method is
> (though that easily becomes clear if you just try it), etcetera....

Are you looking at the
help("extractRawCopyNumbers.CopyNumberChromosomalModel") page?

>
> Is there another place/way I can lookup the documentation of particular
> methods of any kind of class in the aroma packages?

As above, with the disclaimer at the top.  Whenever in doubt, just
drop an email here and ask a question and I'll try to help out.

/Henrik

